meta {
  name: Space Clear Records
  type: http
  seq: 180
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/xrpc/com.atproto.space.clearRecords
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "space": "at:space/did:plc:authorityaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa/org.example.bucket/main",
    "repo": "{{did}}"
  }
}

docs {
  Delete every record in your own repo in a space, as one commit. The repo stays (empty) at a new
  rev, its oplog is cleared, and the space host is told like after any write. In the space
  authority's own repo, the published policy and member records are kept. With nothing to
  delete, nothing is committed.

  Needs a "space:…?action=delete" grant for every collection the repo holds (kept records need
  none). Errors: 400 SpaceNotFound (a deleted or taken-down space), 400 KemKeyNotPublished,
  401 AccountDeactivated / AccountTakedown, 403 Forbidden (repo is not yours),
  403 InsufficientScope, 409 Conflict (a concurrent write; retry).
}
